{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the houses of Egypt shall be full of et the swarm.</b> The reason He repeated a second time <b>et the swarm</b> and did not rely on the mention of the swarm just before it, is that He intended to say that the houses would be filled from the swarm. For if He had not said ״אֶת הֶעָרֹב״ it would have been understood in this manner: ״and the swarm filled the houses of Egypt״ — and accordingly this would be the entire purpose of the plague, that the swarm fill only their houses. But that is not so; rather, first He said <b>I will send against you</b> etc. — meaning, to strike and to destroy — and further He said that the houses would be filled from the swarm. And understand this." "Or it may mean, if He had not said ״אֶת הֶעָרֹב,״ and we had interpreted ״and the swarm filled the houses of Egypt,״ it would have been understood that this is the limit of their multitude — that there would be this boundary, that they fill the houses. But that is not so, for the swarm is very numerous, and the houses will be filled from them but not from all of them. And this is what the verse says in bringing the plague: ״and throughout all the land of Egypt״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:54.790927898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}